notes.lang:
import json

TOOL_SCHEMAS = {
    "lookup_order": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {"order_id": {"type": "string"}},
        "required": ["order_id"],
    }
}

def validate(tool_name, args):
    schema = TOOL_SCHEMAS.get(tool_name)
    if schema is None:
        return False, {"error": "unknown_tool", "tool": tool_name}
    for field in schema["required"]:
        if field not in args:
            return False, {"error": "missing_field", "field": field}
    return True, {}

def dispatch(tool_name, args, tool_choice="auto"):
    if tool_choice == "none":
        return {"answer_from_context": True}
    ok, err = validate(tool_name, args)
    if not ok:
        return {"rejected": True, **err}  # structured, model-actionable
    return {"result": f"stub result for {args}"}  # real impl goes here

notes.body:
Contract-first tool server. Design and implement a tiny tool server exposing three read-only tools with JSON schemas, a validator, tool-choice modes (auto/required/none), and structured error returns. Deliverables: the three schema definitions, the validator and dispatcher code, a log of 20 simulated calls including 5 adversarial ones (wrong types, unknown tools, missing fields), and a one-page write-up of what the validator caught and why each rule exists.

