- **Measuring agent-assisted workflows** — Task completion time and quality vs the unassisted baseline — observed, not self-reported.
- **Defining guardrail metrics** — Refusal correctness, escalation rate, policy-violation count — the safety dials on the dashboard.
- **Escalation design** — Defining when the agent hands to a human, with what context — the safety valve, designed not improvised.
- **Risk registers for agent features** — Each failure mode, its likelihood/impact, mitigations, and owners — written before launch.
- **Rollback plans** — Nondeterministic systems need one-command reverts — deciding the rollback during the incident is too late.
- **Communicating limits to stakeholders** — State plainly what v1 will not do — managed expectations survive contact with reality.

