- **Scoping agent features honestly** — Name the capability boundary: what it handles, what it escalates, what it refuses — in the spec, not the fine print.
- **Build-vs-buy for agent tooling** — Buy the undifferentiated platform; build the workflow-specific layer — weighed against lock-in and team skill.
- **Sequencing low-risk wins first** — Proven value funds harder bets — and early failures are cheap lessons, not visible incidents.
- **Stakeholder alignment** — Agreement on scope, limits, risks, and success metrics before building — the pre-read that prevents surprise.
- **Pricing and cost modeling** — Per-task cost modeled at real volume plus overhead and support — margins that survive the invoice.
- **Launch checklists** — the pre-launch gate: evals green, guardrails instrumented, rollback planned, costs modeled, non-goals agreed — checked before launch, not after.

