- **Onboarding assistants** — Agents that answer new-hire questions from the knowledge base — ramp speed without interrupting the team.
- **Code-review load balancing** — Routing reviews by expertise and load — fairness and speed, with quality still human-judged.
- **1:1 prep agents** — Gathering context (recent work, blockers) so the conversation starts substantive — prep, not replacement.
- **Knowledge-base agents** — Agents that answer new-hire questions from the knowledge base — ramp speed without interrupting the team.
- **Measuring team-health signals** — Review latency, meeting load, after-hours patterns — signals for the manager, not verdicts on people.
- **Privacy boundaries for people data** — Hard lines: no individual surveillance, aggregated signals only, transparent to the team — trust is not a metric to optimize.

