- **The low-code agent landscape** — Platforms offering visual builders, managed models, and connectors — the build-vs-configure spectrum for agents.
- **Copilot Studio basics** — Topics (conversation paths), actions (tool calls), connectors, and deployment — the platform’s vocabulary.
- **What the platform handles for you** — Hosting, model access, auth scaffolding, and monitoring basics — the undifferentiated plumbing.
- **Pricing intuition** — Per-run, per-seat, and message-volume math at your real usage — the bill at scale, not the trial.
- **Choosing a platform** — matching the workflow to the platform's strengths (standard connectors, simple logic) and scoring the trade-aways (portability, customization, cost at scale) before building.
- **When low-code is enough** — Workflow fits the connectors, customization ceiling is above the need, speed beats control — the honest fit test.

