This is the lab sequence — work the steps in order; each one builds on the last.
1. Pick the workflow: real, frequent, annoying — and small enough to finish; write the 'done' criteria first.
2. Build the agent: topics and flows for the happy path first — resist the urge to handle every edge case on day one.
3. Connect the data with scoped connectors from the previous module — no admin credentials, ever.
4. Test with 5 real users: watch them use it; log every failure, confusion, and workaround — the user test is the eval.
5. Gather feedback systematically: 3 questions per user (what worked, what broke, what you'd change); theme the answers.
6. Iterate once: fix the top theme, re-test with 2 users, and show the delta.
7. Write it up: what it automates, the user-test results, the limits — the honest delivery note.

