- **Publishing an agent** — From workspace to shared: environment promotion, config, and smoke tests — the release ritual, low-code edition.
- **Sharing and permissions** — Who can use, who can edit, what data it touches — the access model, set deliberately.
- **Usage monitoring** — Runs, users, errors, and cost — the operational picture after launch.
- **Feedback loops** — User corrections and ratings become the improvement backlog — the system learns from use.
- **Versioning** — saving v1 before the first change and practicing the rollback, so 'deploy' never means 'no way back'.
- **Handoff documentation** — What it does, how it is configured, how to debug it, who owns it — the agent’s afterlife plan.

