- **The customization ceiling** — The point where the platform cannot express what you need — the most important thing to know before building.
- **Escaping to pro-code** — Custom connectors, API fallbacks, or full rebuilds — with your logic and data portable, planned from day one.
- **Vendor lock-in awareness** — Knowing your switching costs: proprietary formats, pricing power, migration effort — assessed upfront.
- **Cost at scale** — Per-run pricing times real volume — the trial is cheap; the enterprise rollout is the real quote.
- **Governance needs** — Data residency, audit, access reviews — the enterprise requirements low-code must still satisfy.
- **Deciding when to graduate** — Ceiling hit, costs ballooning, or governance demands — the signals, watched deliberately.

